{{define "content"}}{{/* API reference (P-12/UX-M03): the in-app, curated
     mirror of docs/api.md's calling surface — auth shape, the headline
     endpoints and one real request/response per family. Visible only to
     principals holding an API-calling scope (cap api); the page is read-only
     and mints nothing. */}}
<header class="head">
  <div class="headcopy">
    <div class="crumb">{{.Org}} / API reference</div>
    <h1>API reference</h1>
    <p class="desc">Everything the dashboard does is available as JSON — these are the endpoints most integrations start from.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="section" id="api-auth">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Authentication</h2></div>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="label">Base URL</span>
    <div class="row"><code class="dev-base-url">{{.Data.BaseURL}}</code><button type="button" class="btn" data-action="copy" data-copy="{{.Data.BaseURL}}">{{icon "copy"}}Copy</button></div>
    <p>Send every request with an API key in the Authorization header:</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>Authorization: Bearer enc_…</code></pre>
    <p class="muted">Keys are issued by an administrator under Access → API keys and carry scopes — a key can call only the endpoints its scopes allow, plus optional model, endpoint, IP and expiry restrictions.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section" id="api-chat">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Chat completions</h2><span class="muted">scope <code>chat.completions</code></span></div>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">OpenAI-compatible chat against a tenant model alias.</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>curl {{.Data.BaseURL}}/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "authorization: Bearer enc_…" -H "content-type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"&lt;model&gt;","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}'</code></pre>
    <pre class="code"><code>{"id":"chatcmpl_…","choices":[{"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"…"},"finish_reason":"stop"}],
 "usage":{"prompt_tokens":4,"completion_tokens":9,"total_tokens":13}}</code></pre>
    <p class="muted"><code>GET /v1/models</code> (scope <code>models.list</code>) lists the model aliases your key may call.</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>curl {{.Data.BaseURL}}/v1/models -H "authorization: Bearer enc_…"</code></pre>
    <pre class="code"><code>{"object":"list","data":[{"id":"model-alias","object":"model"}]}</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section" id="api-embeddings">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Embeddings</h2><span class="muted">scope <code>embeddings.create</code></span></div>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">OpenAI-compatible embeddings for indexing and search pipelines.</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>curl {{.Data.BaseURL}}/v1/embeddings \
  -H "authorization: Bearer enc_…" -H "content-type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"&lt;embedding-model&gt;","input":"text to embed"}'</code></pre>
    <pre class="code"><code>{"object":"list","data":[{"index":0,"embedding":[0.01,…]}],
 "usage":{"prompt_tokens":3,"total_tokens":3}}</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section" id="api-search">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Knowledge search</h2><span class="muted">scope <code>rag</code></span></div>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">Search the collections your identity can read — results carry evidence references back to the source documents.</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>curl {{.Data.BaseURL}}/api/v1/rag/search \
  -H "authorization: Bearer enc_…" -H "content-type: application/json" \
  -d '{"collection_ids":["&lt;collection&gt;"],"query":"invoice total","limit":5}'</code></pre>
    <pre class="code"><code>{"results":[{"content":"…","score":0.82,"document_id":"doc_…"}]}</code></pre>
    <p class="muted">Omitting <code>collection_ids</code> searches every readable collection; more than 20 returns <code>search_scope_too_large</code>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section" id="api-errors">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Errors</h2></div>
  <div class="card">
    <p>Failures return an OpenAI-style envelope — <code>{"error":{"message","type","code"}}</code>. A missing scope is one indistinguishable 403; a budget refusal is <code>budget_exceeded</code>; a model with missing prices is 422 <code>price_missing</code>.</p>
    <p class="muted">Responses (<code>POST /v1/responses</code>, scope <code>responses</code>), extraction (<code>/api/v1/extract/*</code>, scope <code>extract</code>) and the admin surface (<code>/api/v1/admin/*</code>, scope <code>platform.admin</code>) follow the same shape.</p>
  </div>
</div>
{{end}}
